  "adaptations": [
    "Facility roles renamed to forge/counter/alchemy/inn/staff guild. Source effect numbers unchanged.",
    "Original currency identifiers have different enum namespaces. The web game explicitly adopts the selected numeric costs (source currency types 0, 54, and facility 1) as web coins without changing their numbers; this is not a claim about original currency semantics.",
    "5 and 24 are reused as base fantasy item/service prices from the two named source price rows. The product roles and web sale conversion are adaptations.",
    "Source movement numbers are interpreted as world movement speed; production delay numbers are interpreted as seconds.",
    "Stage names and staff display names replaced with original fantasy names.",
    "Magic upgrades, short-range teleport, warrior/archer/mage patron defense, raids and rewards are newly designed web mechanics.",
    "All source numeric values are imported unchanged; web progression conversion/multipliers are applied separately in rules.mjs."
  ],
